item+ function crates/phextron-web/src/json.rs :: display :: pub fn display(&self) -> String { :: Display form, mirroring what the desktop shell's JS produces when it stringifies a JSON value into HTML: strings as themselves, booleans as `true`/`false`, null as empty (callers substitute the em dash where the JS does). Numbers go through their f64 value, because the JS shell stringifies the parsed number, not the wire lexeme: the server emits `8.0`, JSON.parse makes it `8`, and the shell shows `8` — so the WASM renderer shows `8` too. (Rust's `{}` for f64 is the same shortest-round-trip form JS uses at panel magnitudes.) :: doc comment
item+ function crates/phextron-web/src/json.rs :: is_null :: pub fn is_null(&self) -> bool { :: Function is_null takes no inputs beyond the value it is called on, and gives back bool. :: signature
